From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vadik likholetov <vadikas@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 17:51:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: tegra-pkvm: use protected identity DMA

Route host-owned devices through the pKVM identity context instead of
allocating ordinary translated DMA domains. The identity context mirrors
the host stage-2 permissions, so protected guest pages remain inaccessible
while avoiding the translated-domain failure observed on Tegra234.

The AGX pKVM debug target must keep host RAM below the narrowest device DMA
mask while this mode is used.

Signed-off-by: vadik likholetov <vadikas@gmail.com>

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c b/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c
index 57d6563d7..5e1f06a93 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c
@@ -481,7 +481,7 @@ static struct iommu_group *pkvm_tegra_device_group(struct device *dev)
 
 static int pkvm_tegra_default_domain(struct device *dev)
 {
-	return 0;
+	return IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDENTITY;
 }
 
 static const struct iommu_ops pkvm_tegra_iommu_ops = {
@@ -581,15 +581,6 @@ static int pkvm_tegra_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	host_smmu->id = pkvm_tegra_smmu_current;
 	host_smmu->address_bits = min3(hyp_smmu->ias, hyp_smmu->oas,
 				       get_kvm_ipa_limit());
-	/*
-	 * Keep the pKVM bring-up DMA aperture below 4 GiB.  Tegra234 clients
-	 * using the top of their 39-bit DMA mask currently reach the memory
-	 * controller as 0xffffffff00 without raising a context-bank fault,
-	 * while clients allocated in the 32-bit aperture translate normally.
-	 * Preserve the SMMU's full output address size so buffers may remain
-	 * above 4 GiB; this limit applies only to device-visible IOVAs.
-	 */
-	host_smmu->address_bits = min(host_smmu->address_bits, 32U);
 	host_smmu->mc = devm_tegra_memory_controller_get(dev);
 	if (IS_ERR(host_smmu->mc))
 		return PTR_ERR(host_smmu->mc);
-- 
